./.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap19/review_pass1_supported.log:4105:- algorithm summary: `stmap18` keeps the classic `map` SCL genlib gain default of `250` and passes `fSkipFanout = 19` into the mapper. Mode `19` preserves the `stmap17` mode `18` lower-moderate fanout bucket, tight-depth window, adaptive profile gate, guard-stat counters, admitted-relief diagnostics, and timing-quality discriminator. The only source-level behavior change is diagnostic: when a middle-slack candidate is rejected because the stricter two-inverter fallback is active, but the candidate would have cleared the one-inverter area threshold, mode `19` increments a near-miss counter and prints up to 128 `stmap18 near-miss diag` lines. Existing `map` and `stmap0` through `stmap17` behavior are preserved because modes `0` through `18` retain their previous meanings.
