codex
The mapper changes appear buildable, but the patch leaves a non-restartable live campaign state in tracked artifacts and has a concrete diagnostic overcount in the new stmap19 early-seed counter. These should be fixed before treating the patch as correct.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Do not commit agent-running campaign state — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/.autoeda/runtime/campaign_state.json:9-9
  When these runtime artifacts are committed and later resumed from a clean checkout, `status: "agent-running"` is stale machine-local state; `supervisor.yaml` does not list `agent-running` as restartable, and the associated launcher PID/log can make automation treat the campaign as still in progress instead of advancing or recovering. Reset this to the appropriate completed/restartable state before committing the iteration artifacts.

- [P3] Count only relaxed early-seed admissions — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:541-542
  When `stmap19` admits a pre-profile middle-slack candidate through the existing two-inverter fallback, for example `!fArrivalQuality` but `AreaSave > 2 * AreaInv`, this unconditional `!fProfileOpen` increment reports it as an early seed even though the new one-inverter timing-quality rule did not fire. That overcounts the `early-seed` diagnostics on those inputs and can mislead the next iteration analysis; gate the counter on the relaxed/arrival-quality path.
The mapper changes appear buildable, but the patch leaves a non-restartable live campaign state in tracked artifacts and has a concrete diagnostic overcount in the new stmap19 early-seed counter. These should be fixed before treating the patch as correct.

